From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0023] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: a chapter person file too big for the read is laid in memory

A patched chapter person file that does not fit in the stored size was
kept original (Seal of Flames R013, R023: 930/921 and 1128/1118 bytes,
round 59 check). Like a placement file, it is now laid in memory at the
first system call after the game stored it: found in the Person archive
list (0x006D3B28: {data start, ArchiveFile*, next}) by its archive name,
guarded cell by cell (apply_file). Person::Load runs before the chapter's
placements are read, so the cells are in place before the units are
made. The single placement wait becomes one wait per file. Round 60,
track sealfix: docs/tests/SEAL_SAVE.md 8.
